    "Real World Abuse": "",
    "Scenario 1": "Developer creates application token from user_id (predictable integer). User 1 receives token \"1\", user 2 receives token \"2\". Attacker intercepts own token, increments by 1, accesses next user's session. Enumerates all user tokens by incrementing. Exports all user sessions.",
    "Scenario 2": "Application generates session tokens from timestamp (predictable). Attacker logs in, captures token. Calculates token for user's session at specific timestamp. Predicts admin token by calculating time of admin login. Forges admin session token. Gains administrative access.",
