    "Detection Opportunities": "- Unusual token patterns during pattern analysis\n- Successful session access without corresponding login\n- Token reuse across multiple sessions\n- Tokens older than expected lifetime still accepting requests\n- Multiple sessions from same token\n- Sequential/predictable token enumeration attacks\n- Session tokens appearing in logs/error messages\n- Tokens transmitted over unencrypted channels",
    "Security Recommendations": "- Use cryptographically secure random token generation (urandom, /dev/urandom)\n- Implement strong session token standard (minimum 128-bit entropy)\n- Use framework-provided session management (avoid custom implementations)\n- Invalidate tokens after fixed timeout (30 minutes typical)\n- Implement absolute session timeout\n- Bind tokens to specific IP address (conditional)\n- Regenerate token after authentication\n- Validate token signature and integrity\n- Implement session fixation protection\n- Use secure cookie attributes (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite)\n- Implement logout invalidating token\n- Monitor for token reuse\n- Implement rate limiting on token validation\n- Use JWT with secure algorithm (RS256, not HS256 with weak secret)\n- Avoid exposing token generation logic",
