    "Why It Exists": "- Token generation using weak randomness\n- Tokens never expire or expire after excessive time (24+ hours)\n- Token reuse across multiple reset attempts\n- Token validation bypassed through manipulation\n- Token structure revealing predictable patterns\n- Insufficient token entropy\n- No rate limiting on reset attempts",
    "Attacker Interest": "Critical",
    "Discovery Methods": "- Password reset flow testing\n- Token analysis (predictability testing)\n- Token reuse attempts\n- Token timing analysis\n- Intercepted token examination\n- Brute-force token enumeration\n- Token manipulation (changing user ID component)\n- Intercepted email credential analysis\n- Social engineering password reset",
