    "Real World Abuse": "",
    "Scenario 1": "GitHub search reveals \"aws_access_key_id\" in public repositories. Attacker finds 147 AWS keys in source code. Tests them. 89 still valid. Uses keys to enumerate EC2 instances. Finds production database snapshots. Extracts all customer data.",
    "Scenario 2": "SaaS application uses AWS API key for document storage. API key never rotates. Stored in application.properties in version control. Attacker obtains key. Uses AWS CLI to enumerate S3 buckets. Finds bucket containing daily database backups. Downloads all backups.",
